# Where storage is taken from a memory file's arena without an entity to
# describe it, and what each such place is doing.
#
# Derived by tests/check-raw-allocations.sh: every call to
# xpost_memory_file_alloc outside the allocator's own file, named by the
# function it sits in. The one call the derivation leaves out is the one
# inside xpost_memory_table_alloc, which is how an entity gets its storage
# and is the route that does record a row.
#
# disposition  file  function  reason
#
#   settled  a block with no row that a rearrangement of the arena may
#            nonetheless step over, for the reason given.
#   blocks   a block with no row, and nothing can find it: no size, no tag,
#            and no way to reach whatever holds its address. While one of
#            these stands, the arena cannot be rearranged at all, because a
#            pass that walked the table would relocate a live entity onto
#            storage it could not see.

settled  xpost_context.c   initglobal   the reservation at the foot of global virtual memory: it is the first allocation the bank makes, so it lies below every entity and no rearrangement reaches it, and nothing addresses it -- it exists so that the low addresses, which every link in this tree spells "absent" as zero, are never handed out as live storage
settled  xpost_context.c   initlocal    the same reservation at the foot of local virtual memory, made the same way and for the same reason

blocks  xpost_stack.c     xpost_stack_init            a stack segment. Every stack in virtual memory is one of these -- the operand, execution, dictionary and hold stacks, the name stack, and the record stack a save owns -- and each segment names the next and the previous by address, so a segment that moved would orphan the rest of its chain
